{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-98881192a3ce53b9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstrat_id: RHAISTRAT-9011\n3\ttitle: Adopt structured JSON logging across RHOAI components\n4\tstatus: Refinement Done\n5\tpriority: Major\n6\tlabels:\n7\t- refined\n8\t- observability\n9\tlinks: []\n10\t---\n11\t\n12\t## Problem Statement\n13\t\n14\tRHOAI components log in inconsistent formats — plain text, key=value, and\n15\tad-hoc JSON — which breaks centralized log queries and makes support cases\n16\texpensive: correlating one user request across Dashboard, serving, and\n17\tpipelines requires per-component parsing rules. The platform needs one\n18\tstructured logging convention, and each component needs to adopt it. Component\n19\tadoptions are independent of each other once the convention exists.\n20\t\n21\t## High-Level Requirements\n22\t\n23\t| ID | Priority | Requirement |\n24\t|--------|----------|-------------|\n25\t| HLR-1  | P0 | A platform logging convention is published: JSON schema, required fields (timestamp, level, component, namespace, correlation id), and library guidance per language (Go, Python, TypeScript). |\n26\t| HLR-2  | P0 | Dashboard emits convention-conformant logs. |\n27\t| HLR-3  | P0 | KServe controller and serving runtimes emit convention-conformant logs. |\n28\t| HLR-4  | P1 | Data Science Pipelines (operator and API server) emits convention-conformant logs. |\n29\t| HLR-5  | P1 | Model Registry emits convention-conformant logs. |\n30\t| HLR-6  | P1 | TrustyAI services emit convention-conformant logs. |\n31\t| HLR-7  | P1 | Notebooks (notebook-controller) emits convention-conformant logs. |\n32\t| HLR-8  | P2 | Training Operator emits convention-conformant logs. |\n33\t| HLR-9  | P2 | Documentation describes the log format and example queries for common support scenarios. |\n34\t\n35\t## Affected Components\n36\t\n37\t- Dashboard\n38\t- KServe\n39\t- Data Science Pipelines\n40\t- Model Registry\n41\t- TrustyAI\n42\t- Notebooks\n43\t- Training Operator\n44\t\n45\t## Out of Scope\n46\t\n47\t- Log storage, retention, or forwarding infrastructure\n48\t- Metrics and tracing conventions (logging only)\n49\t\n50\t## Open Questions\n51\t\n52\tNone — the convention work (HLR-1) is prerequisite design, and per-component\n53\tadoptions are mechanical once it lands.\n54\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ba310ff93a4ce5ff","agent_id":"a430fed9f97194460","session_id":"3eca0caa-e3c9-4b4a-8579-02aaafb311df","uuid":"7f1e6d52-34ba-45cf-827a-74d162df3458","timestamp":"2026-10-21T20:39:32.439Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-98881192a3ce53b9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9011"}
