10 |\n99\t\n100\tAll nine HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements. Priority inheritance:\n101\tE001 is directly P0 (HLR-1) and also blocks all P0 adoptions, so it is P0 by\n102\tboth routes.\n103\t\n104\t## Health Warnings\n105\t\n106\t1. **Missing strategy sections.** The strategy has no Impacted Teams table, no\n107\t   Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then Acceptance Criteria, and no\n108\t   Non-Functional Requirements. Teams were derived from architecture context\n109\t   owning-team fields; epic acceptance criteria were derived from HLR text.\n110\t   Human verification of team assignments is recommended.\n111\t2. **Assumed team ownership.** The convention epic (E001, team \"RHOAI\n112\t   Platform\") and the documentation epic (E010, team \"RHOAI Documentation\")\n113\t   have no team stated anywhere in the strategy or architecture context.\n114\t3. **Docs priority inversion (expected per rules).** E010 is P1 (docs-authoring\n115\t   exception: strategy priority Major → P1) although HLR-9 is P2. Additionally,\n116\t   Rule 11 blocks E010 on all Implementations, including the P2 Training\n117\t   Operator adoption (E009) — the P1 docs epic cannot complete until the\n118\t   lowest-priority adoption lands. If Training Operator slips, docs slip with\n119\t   it; consider descope options at planning time.\n120\t4. **Midstream rebase risk (not a dependency).** Most adoptions land in\n121\t   midstream forks of upstream projects (opendatahub-io/kserve,\n122\t   data-science-pipelines-operator, model-registry, kubeflow notebook-controller\n123\t   fork, training-operator). These are coordination risks, not DAG edges; no\n124\t   upstream contribution is required by the strategy.\n125\t5. **Serving runtimes scope breadth.** E004 spans multiple model-execution\n126\t   runtimes (vLLM, OpenVINO, Caikit) with heterogeneous logging stacks. The\n127\t   strategy treats them as one component; if per-runtime divergence proves\n128\t   large, the implementing team may need to split delivery internally.\n129\t\n130\t## Tiered Delivery\n131\t\n132\tNot applicable. There are no external dependencies with uncertain timing: the\n133\tconvention is internal work and all adoption targets are platform components.\n134\tThe natural staging (convention first, adoptions in parallel, docs last) is\n135\talready captured by the DAG.\n136\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8bb366f4b5f61a13","agent_id":"aecfa8e6b847ca9a9","session_id":"3eca0caa-e3c9-4b4a-8579-02aaafb311df","uuid":"afad5743-862c-48b3-848d-44b3372c7f9c","timestamp":"2026-10-21T20:55:59.630Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8784074842cec546","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9011 decomposition"}
