{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-92c97b6203914f08","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9011-E001\n3\ttitle: Publish platform structured JSON logging convention\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9011\n5\tcomponent: Platform Operator\n6\tteam: RHOAI Platform\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 1\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: -1\n14\t  open_questions: 1\n15\t  external_dependency: 1\n16\t  human_process_gates: -1\n17\t  repo_access: 0\n18\t  architecture_claims: 0\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: Medium\n23\tai_implementability_score: 1\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Publish platform structured JSON logging convention\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers the platform-wide structured logging convention that all\n34\tRHOAI component logging adoptions build against: a JSON log-record schema with\n35\trequired fields, and per-language library guidance so that component teams\n36\tproduce conformant output without re-inventing the design. It is the\n37\tprerequisite design work for every per-component adoption in the strategy.\n38\t\n39\t## Scope\n40\t\n41\t- Define the JSON log-record schema: valid JSON per log line, with required\n42\t  fields `timestamp`, `level`, `component`, `namespace`, and `correlation id`.\n43\t- Provide library guidance for each language used by affected components —\n44\t  Go, Python, and TypeScript: which structured logging approach to use and\n45\t  how to emit records that validate against the schema.\n46\t- Define how the correlation id is populated so a single user request can be\n47\t  correlated across components (Dashboard, serving, pipelines) without\n48\t  per-component parsing rules.\n49\t- Publish the convention where adopting teams can reference it, and obtain\n50\t  review/sign-off from the owning teams of the adopting components.\n51\t\n52\t## Acceptance Criteria\n53\t\n54\t- A published convention document defines the JSON log-record schema, and the\n55\t  schema requires the fields `timestamp`, `level`, `component`, `namespace`,\n56\t  and `correlation id`.\n57\t- A sample record validating against the schema can be produced for each of\n58\t  Go, Python, and TypeScript using the documented library guidance.\n59\t- The convention defines correlation-id population rules sufficient to\n60\t  correlate one user request across Dashboard, serving, and pipelines.\n61\t- The convention is reviewed and acknowledged by the owning teams of the\n62\t  components listed in the strategy's affected components (Dashboard, KServe,\n63\t  Data Science Pipelines, Model Registry, TrustyAI, Notebooks, Training\n64\t  Operator, plus the serving runtimes).\n65\t- Out of scope is respected: no log storage, retention, forwarding, metrics,\n66\t  or tracing conventions are introduced.\n67\t\n68\t## HLR Traceability\n69\t\n70\t- HLR-1 (P0): A platform logging convention is published: JSON schema,\n71\t  required fields, and library guidance per language.\n72\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aee6fcae0e5016d2","agent_id":"a8c14d8119b0dbce3","session_id":"3eca0caa-e3c9-4b4a-8579-02aaafb311df","uuid":"d211d84a-c50f-4f3e-b098-d89a0f94185a","timestamp":"2026-10-21T20:57:14.746Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-92c97b6203914f08","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9011 decomposition"}
