{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a031204dd5ef0ccb","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9011-E002\n3\ttitle: Adopt structured JSON logging in Dashboard\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9011\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9011-E001\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 0\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 1\n17\t  external_dependency: 1\n18\t  human_process_gates: 0\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 0\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 5\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Adopt structured JSON logging in Dashboard\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tConvert the Dashboard (odh-dashboard, TypeScript) to emit logs conformant to\n35\tthe published platform structured JSON logging convention, so Dashboard log\n36\tlines can be queried centrally alongside other components and correlated with\n37\tserving and pipelines activity by correlation id.\n38\t\n39\t## Scope\n40\t\n41\t- Replace existing Dashboard logging (plain text / ad-hoc formats) with\n42\t  structured JSON output that validates against the platform log-record\n43\t  schema, including the required fields timestamp, level, component,\n44\t  namespace, and correlation id.\n45\t- Follow the TypeScript library guidance from the platform convention.\n46\t- Propagate the correlation id on user-initiated operations where the\n47\t  Dashboard is the entry point, so downstream serving and pipelines log lines\n48\t  can be correlated back to the originating request.\n49\t\n50\t## Acceptance Criteria\n51\t\n52\t- All Dashboard log output is valid JSON per the platform convention schema,\n53\t  with all required fields present.\n54\t- A support-style query on the required fields (e.g., by correlation id)\n55\t  returns Dashboard log lines for a user request without component-specific\n56\t  parsing rules.\n57\t- The change is rollback-safe: a documented revert or gating path exists so\n58\t  support tooling relying on the previous format is not broken unrecoverably.\n59\t- The Dashboard build pipeline remains green.\n60\t\n61\t## HLR Traceability\n62\t\n63\t- HLR-2 (P0): Dashboard emits convention-conformant logs.\n64\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aee6fcae0e5016d2","agent_id":"a8c14d8119b0dbce3","session_id":"3eca0caa-e3c9-4b4a-8579-02aaafb311df","uuid":"b8a80d8d-e2b1-46be-8335-f08ca3fa1ad4","timestamp":"2026-10-21T20:57:15.788Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a031204dd5ef0ccb","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9011 decomposition"}
